WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.110
Instructor: All right, so it's time

00:01.110 --> 00:04.800
for an exercise to get some practice with Git branches.

00:04.800 --> 00:07.320
So this is going to be a simple exercise

00:07.320 --> 00:09.360
in terms of the files we're working with.

00:09.360 --> 00:11.550
Kind of silly, it's Harry Potter themed,

00:11.550 --> 00:14.460
but it doesn't matter if you know Harry Potter or don't.

00:14.460 --> 00:15.810
If you just follow the instructions

00:15.810 --> 00:18.660
and make the branches when you're prompted to make branches,

00:18.660 --> 00:20.700
and switch branches when you're prompted to switch,

00:20.700 --> 00:22.080
you should be good to go.

00:22.080 --> 00:24.750
Now the theme of this, aside from Harry Potter,

00:24.750 --> 00:28.620
is of Harry Potter patronuses, which are like,

00:28.620 --> 00:31.290
I guess a Harry Potter version of a spirit animal.

00:31.290 --> 00:33.090
If you've seen the movie or read the books,

00:33.090 --> 00:34.920
the spell Expecto Patronum,

00:34.920 --> 00:36.300
I don't even know why I'm going into it.

00:36.300 --> 00:37.133
It doesn't matter.

00:37.133 --> 00:39.930
Anyway, wizards have their own patronus, different animals.

00:39.930 --> 00:42.150
So you will be putting some animals

00:42.150 --> 00:46.710
in files on different branches for different characters.

00:46.710 --> 00:49.260
Okay, so again, I strongly recommend you do this

00:49.260 --> 00:50.093
on your own.

00:50.093 --> 00:51.030
Follow the instructions.

00:51.030 --> 00:54.750
You can find this file linked to in the resources

00:54.750 --> 00:55.950
for this video.

00:55.950 --> 00:57.360
You're going to make a new directory,

00:57.360 --> 00:59.100
make a new git repo inside of it.

00:59.100 --> 01:00.750
Make sure you're not already in one.

01:00.750 --> 01:04.410
Then you'll create a new file called patronus.txt,

01:04.410 --> 01:06.060
and you'll leave it empty for now.

01:06.060 --> 01:08.940
So this will be on your default branch, the master branch,

01:08.940 --> 01:11.730
or if you've changed the default name, whatever it is, main.

01:11.730 --> 01:14.880
But for now, the default is just master.

01:14.880 --> 01:17.310
Then we'll make our first commit with this message,

01:17.310 --> 01:19.290
add empty patronus file.

01:19.290 --> 01:22.050
Then we'll make a new branch called Harry.

01:22.050 --> 01:25.020
And at the same time, or on the next line,

01:25.020 --> 01:27.420
a second new branch called snape.

01:27.420 --> 01:29.730
Both of them should be based on the master branch.

01:29.730 --> 01:32.580
They should contain this empty patronus file.

01:32.580 --> 01:35.820
Then you will move to the harry branch that you just made.

01:35.820 --> 01:37.800
And there are two different ways we've talked about

01:37.800 --> 01:41.130
for moving to new branches or moving between branches.

01:41.130 --> 01:44.460
So I would like you to use the new command.

01:44.460 --> 01:46.860
If you don't remember which one is new and old,

01:46.860 --> 01:47.693
it's not a big deal.

01:47.693 --> 01:49.470
Just use one of the commands that we talked about,

01:49.470 --> 01:53.490
and then later on use the other command that you didn't use.

01:53.490 --> 01:57.450
Okay, so on the harry branch we are going to put this inside

01:57.450 --> 01:58.560
of the patronus file,

01:58.560 --> 02:00.780
Harry Potter's patronus is a stag.

02:00.780 --> 02:04.170
So copy all of this and put it in that file,

02:04.170 --> 02:06.210
save it, add and commit the changes,

02:06.210 --> 02:08.190
and then use this message,

02:08.190 --> 02:09.780
add harry's stag patronus,

02:09.780 --> 02:12.360
and again this is on the harry branch.

02:12.360 --> 02:14.100
Then you will move over

02:14.100 --> 02:17.310
to the other branch you already made called snape.

02:17.310 --> 02:20.160
So this branch, again, should be based off of master

02:20.160 --> 02:21.390
when you made it early on,

02:21.390 --> 02:23.490
at the same time as the harry branch.

02:23.490 --> 02:26.100
When you move over to that branch, use the other command,

02:26.100 --> 02:29.730
the older command to switch or to change branches.

02:29.730 --> 02:32.580
And then open up the patronus file again.

02:32.580 --> 02:34.530
and this time, put this in there,

02:34.530 --> 02:36.540
Snape's patronus is a doe.

02:36.540 --> 02:38.220
So this is what you'll put in there.

02:38.220 --> 02:42.180
Save it, add and commit, and then use this message

02:42.180 --> 02:43.560
if you'd like.

02:43.560 --> 02:45.480
Then something different.

02:45.480 --> 02:49.230
We will make a new branch based upon the snape branch,

02:49.230 --> 02:51.003
and we're going to call it lily.

02:51.960 --> 02:53.520
If you don't know any of these characters,

02:53.520 --> 02:54.720
it really doesn't matter.

02:54.720 --> 02:56.220
All you need to know is that Snape and Lily

02:56.220 --> 02:57.750
have the same patronus.

02:57.750 --> 02:59.910
So we are branching off of snape

02:59.910 --> 03:01.590
to a new branch called lily.

03:01.590 --> 03:03.390
And then we will move to that branch,

03:03.390 --> 03:06.870
to the lily branch, and we'll edit this file.

03:06.870 --> 03:08.340
And we're gonna keep the doe in there

03:08.340 --> 03:09.840
because they have the same patronus,

03:09.840 --> 03:12.030
but we will edit this little header

03:12.030 --> 03:15.630
so that it says LILY'S PATRONUS instead of SNAPE'S.

03:15.630 --> 03:17.430
You can leave the doe alone, that's the point.

03:17.430 --> 03:19.890
They share the same patronus, the same form.

03:19.890 --> 03:21.570
Then you'll add and commit.

03:21.570 --> 03:23.010
You can use this message if you want.

03:23.010 --> 03:24.810
So this is on the lily branch.

03:24.810 --> 03:27.480
Then run a command to list all the branches,

03:27.480 --> 03:28.590
you should see four.

03:28.590 --> 03:30.660
So just making sure you remember that command.

03:30.660 --> 03:33.750
And then as a bonus, delete the snape branch.

03:33.750 --> 03:35.220
Poor Snape.

03:35.220 --> 03:39.630
Okay, so if you're still here, I really recommend,

03:39.630 --> 03:42.150
I insist that you try it on your own,

03:42.150 --> 03:45.030
but if you wanna just watch me do it, here we go.

03:45.030 --> 03:47.380
So I'm gonna make a new folder called patronus.

03:48.750 --> 03:52.770
Let's just do that here, patronus. I'll cd into it.

03:52.770 --> 03:54.150
I'm going to initialize a repo,

03:54.150 --> 03:56.220
but first make sure I'm not in one.

03:56.220 --> 03:59.400
Okay, so now I have this folder

03:59.400 --> 04:00.690
and a new repo in it,

04:00.690 --> 04:03.753
and I'm gonna create a file called patronus.txt,

04:04.650 --> 04:07.233
patronus.txt.

04:08.880 --> 04:11.910
And then I'm going to add and commit with this message,

04:11.910 --> 04:14.250
add empty patronus file.

04:14.250 --> 04:19.170
So git add that file, git commit -m, there's my message,

04:19.170 --> 04:20.220
and there we go.

04:20.220 --> 04:21.630
That's the first bit.

04:21.630 --> 04:24.120
Now immediately make a new branch called harry

04:24.120 --> 04:26.010
and another new branch called snape,

04:26.010 --> 04:27.930
both based on the master branch.

04:27.930 --> 04:31.290
I'm currently on master, so that works to our advantage.

04:31.290 --> 04:33.750
I'm going to make a new branch called harry

04:33.750 --> 04:35.343
and another one called snape.

04:36.690 --> 04:38.730
Okay, next step,

04:38.730 --> 04:42.090
move to the harry branch using the new way of doing it.

04:42.090 --> 04:44.520
The new command is git switch.

04:44.520 --> 04:48.570
So we'll move over using git switch to the harry branch,

04:48.570 --> 04:51.270
and now we see that we're on harry.

04:51.270 --> 04:54.150
Then in the patronus file, add the following.

04:54.150 --> 04:56.610
So I need to open up that file.

04:56.610 --> 04:59.340
So I'll do, I copied all of that first of all,

04:59.340 --> 05:02.160
but then I'll use my code shortcut, code,

05:02.160 --> 05:03.660
just do the whole folder.

05:03.660 --> 05:05.430
Here's that patronus file.

05:05.430 --> 05:07.620
I will paste that in there.

05:07.620 --> 05:08.700
Lemme zoom out a bit.

05:08.700 --> 05:11.160
Okay, so I'll save that.

05:11.160 --> 05:12.570
And then it wants me to add

05:12.570 --> 05:15.900
and commit the changes with this commit message.

05:15.900 --> 05:19.380
Alright, so we'll do a git add patronus,

05:19.380 --> 05:24.380
git commit -m, and paste in that message.

05:25.457 --> 05:28.383
Okay, so we should now have two commits on this branch.

05:29.520 --> 05:32.280
Next we are going to move over to the snape branch

05:32.280 --> 05:36.330
using the other, the older command, which is git checkout.

05:36.330 --> 05:40.440
So we'll do that, git checkout snape.

05:40.440 --> 05:43.530
You could use switch, right, they're both gonna work,

05:43.530 --> 05:45.570
but I just want you to get practice with both.

05:45.570 --> 05:49.500
So I'm now on the snape branch as my terminal tells me,

05:49.500 --> 05:53.043
and I'm going to put this in the patronus file.

05:54.120 --> 05:56.460
Now if I take a look, the patronus file is empty, right?

05:56.460 --> 05:58.080
Because I branched off of master

05:58.080 --> 05:59.670
before anything was in here.

05:59.670 --> 06:03.000
I didn't branch from the Harry Potter or the harry branch.

06:03.000 --> 06:06.760
Okay, I'll save that and then I'm gonna make a new commit

06:07.830 --> 06:09.813
with that change and this message.

06:11.610 --> 06:15.780
Okay, so git add patronus, git commit -m

06:15.780 --> 06:19.443
on the snape branch, add snape's doe patronus.

06:20.520 --> 06:22.440
And then I need to make a new branch

06:22.440 --> 06:26.613
based on the snape branch called lily, and then move to it.

06:27.510 --> 06:30.120
So I could just do git branch lily,

06:30.120 --> 06:32.220
I'm on snape and that's where I should be

06:32.220 --> 06:35.700
if I want to branch based on snape, I want this history.

06:35.700 --> 06:40.200
Just to remind you, if I do a git log, two commits,

06:40.200 --> 06:43.140
add empty file, add snape's doe patronus.

06:43.140 --> 06:46.290
So if I do a git branch lily, that will work.

06:46.290 --> 06:49.260
Or I can make the branch and switch to it in one go

06:49.260 --> 06:53.100
like this, git switch -c lily,

06:53.100 --> 06:55.320
and that made it and it switched me over.

06:55.320 --> 06:58.830
I still see add snape's doe patronus, right?

06:58.830 --> 07:01.170
The file contains the doe.

07:01.170 --> 07:02.460
Now I'm going to edit it

07:02.460 --> 07:05.763
so that it says LILY'S PATRONUS instead of SNAPE'S.

07:06.630 --> 07:09.933
So I'll put that up top and then I will add and commit.

07:10.920 --> 07:15.920
So just copy this message, git status, we modified patronus,

07:17.490 --> 07:21.330
so we add, we commit and we'll give it that message.

07:21.330 --> 07:24.240
Okay, next, and almost at the end,

07:24.240 --> 07:27.690
run a git command to list all branches, we should see four.

07:27.690 --> 07:29.100
So what is that command?

07:29.100 --> 07:31.320
It's just git branch and nothing else.

07:31.320 --> 07:35.790
Just git branch, we see four, I'm currently on lily.

07:35.790 --> 07:39.297
And then, bonus, delete the snape branch.

07:39.297 --> 07:41.250
Oh, poor Snape.

07:41.250 --> 07:43.140
Well, to delete a branch,

07:43.140 --> 07:46.563
we saw that we use the exact same command, git branch,

07:48.270 --> 07:49.470
and then a branch name.

07:49.470 --> 07:53.640
But we pass in this -d, git branch -d,

07:53.640 --> 07:55.770
and then snape, that's the name of the branch.

07:55.770 --> 07:57.180
Make sure I'm not on that branch.

07:57.180 --> 07:58.800
I'm currently not.

07:58.800 --> 08:01.050
And there we go, it was deleted.

08:01.050 --> 08:03.600
So now if I do just regular git branch,

08:03.600 --> 08:05.550
only three branches.

08:05.550 --> 08:06.780
And that's it, that's the end

08:06.780 --> 08:09.393
of the branching exercise, okay.
